1
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:30,420
paradise of the world is a paradise

2
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:37,817
I'm going to take my hand
on my hand I'm going to take

3
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:43,897
my hand on the road I'm going

4
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:46,177
to take my

5
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:51,020
hand on the road

6
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,000
Let's go.

7
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:34,677
Aru Kunemon and Mamemon searched all
over for the legendary Destiny Stone.

8
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:38,397
Once they found it, Aru Kunemon
created Nightmon to destroy it.

9
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:42,980
But our guy's DNA digiballed, and
we were able to stop him. Meanwhile,

10
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:47,237
Agumon confronted Black War Greymon and
tried to convince him to be his friend.

11
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,337
Yeah, good luck.

12
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:51,257
But just as Black Mork
Greymon was coming around,

13
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:54,117
he got this weird feeling and
left to find the Destiny Stone.

14
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,517
There was nothing we could do.

15
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:59,277
We had to watch as Black Mork
Greymon destroyed the Destiny Stone.

16
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:01,536
Is this the end of the digital world?

17
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,800
Today's miyako is today's miyako!

18
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:17,750
Yay!

19
00:02:17,833 --> 00:02:19,800
I'm finally in Kyoto! Yo, Lee!

20
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:21,417
Hurry or you'll miss the bus!

21
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:22,330
I'm coming!

22
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,788
Dear Poromon and Izzy,
how's it going, guys?

23
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:30,377
This is the second day of our school
trip and we're finally in Kyoto.

24
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:32,417
I'm having a great time with my friends.

25
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,559
What a cool place!

26
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,080
And the food is fab.

27
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:37,257
Poromon, if you're good,
I'll bring you a souvenir.

28
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:38,170
Come here.

29
00:02:38,253 --> 00:02:39,083
Ciao for now. Yelly.

30
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:42,077
According to everything
you've just told me,

31
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:45,017
this whole mess started when
your digivice changed into a D3.

32
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:48,097
If my calculations are
correct, it's all your fault.

33
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:49,010
Huh?

34
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:51,817
The others needed D3s in
order to compete with you,

35
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:55,537
so their subconscious minds must have
somehow willed their digivices to change.

36
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:58,177
Although I'm not sure Davis
has a subconscious mind.

37
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:01,800
As strong as these digivices
are, they just weren't enough.

38
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:03,250
Of course,

39
00:03:03,333 --> 00:03:06,117
that also means you must have made a wish
for your digivice to change into a D3.

40
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:08,260
I don't remember making any wishes.

41
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:12,919
In fact, I always got the short side
of the wishbone from the turkey.

42
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,077
Like I said, it must have
been your subconscious.

43
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,757
We geniuses have pretty big ones.

44
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,057
In the digital world, data
is formed into shapes,

45
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:21,797
usually based on whatever a person
has running through their mind,

46
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,637
kind of like a VCR for the brain.

47
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,897
And that's the reason
why everyone's clothes

48
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:28,097
change every time they go
into the digital world,

49
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:32,298
and why Davis looks the way he does,
like a fighter pilot on a safari.

50
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:34,870
I see.

51
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:38,631
So then I must have wished for
that Digimon Emperor outfit.

52
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:41,060
So you're not perfect.

53
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:45,097
You should read Singvold's
Theory of Ultimate Brain Power.

54
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:47,768
You might be able to
pick up a few pointers.

55
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:50,121
Actually, I taught a class on it.

56
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:54,535
But don't you think Tesoro's strengthening
your mind was more effective?

57
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,240
Uh, yeah.

58
00:03:56,500 --> 00:04:00,157
But of course Gorski's My Brain My
Buddy is the quintessential masterpiece

59
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,017
when it comes to exploring the
inner workings of the human mind.

60
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:04,777
I'm sure you've read it a dozen times.

61
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:07,397
It's a bestseller in the school's
psychology department bookstore.

62
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,600
I'm sorry, Izzy.

63
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,997
I can't believe I've
never heard of that one.

64
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,860
I feel so ashamed of myself.

65
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:14,941
Oh, don't worry.

66
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:16,997
I've got an extra copy you can borrow.

67
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:20,374
After all, we high IQ types
gotta stick together, right?

68
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:21,370
Besides,

69
00:04:21,453 --> 00:04:24,817
of all the other DigiDestined I've met,
you're one of the only ones as smart as me.

70
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:25,817
Other DigiDestined?

71
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:27,477
What are you talking about, huh?

72
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:31,325
Oh, I guess no one told you that
we're not the only ones around.

73
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:34,617
Actually, there are quite a
few of us all over the world.

74
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:37,641
I haven't met them all
yet, but I'm working on it.

75
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:40,877
It seems that most of us
have one thing in common.

76
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,437
We had some kind of
encounter with the Digimon

77
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:46,057
when they invaded the real
world a few years ago.

78
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:49,220
And now we each have
our own Digimon partner.

79
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:51,930
I see.

80
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,201
That means that I must have, too.

81
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:58,218
Everything from that time
is still such a blur to me.

82
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:04,540
Oh, Poromon, there's an email here
for you from Yoli on her trip.

83
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,357
Hey, what's wrong with you?

84
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:07,360
Are you sick?

85
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:10,650
Oh,

86
00:05:10,733 --> 00:05:12,817
he's just really tired
because he's been here in

87
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:15,777
the real world for a couple
of days without Yoli.

88
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:20,040
I know sometimes when Ken's not
here, even my naps make me exhausted.

89
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,977
Yoli asked me to watch him while
she was on her school trip,

90
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:25,237
and it's been three days since she left.

91
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,937
I've noticed that as each day passes,

92
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:29,837
he seems to get more and more
tired, and he's not very hungry.

93
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:30,750
You know,

94
00:05:30,833 --> 00:05:32,237
it's really got to be bad when he'd rather

95
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:34,657
sleep than eat a bag of
chocolate gummy chews.

96
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:35,570
Well,

97
00:05:35,653 --> 00:05:36,483
then I'll just have to
take him to the digital

98
00:05:36,566 --> 00:05:38,597
world so that he can regain his strength.

99
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:41,997
Davis and the others have already
gone on ahead, haven't they?

100
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:42,957
Yeah, you're right.

101
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,177
That's a good idea, Ken.

102
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,090
Here you go.

103
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:47,897
Things are kind of crazy there
now, so be careful of any warps.

104
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:50,857
Promise me you won't talk
to any strange Digimon.

105
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:51,900
I'll be fine.

106
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:57,172
Hey, Izzy, do you think I can ever make
up for all the trouble I've caused?

107
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:00,558
Oh, look, Ken, we all make mistakes.

108
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:05,517
When we first went to the digital world,
I came up with a bunch of theories.

109
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,137
Not all of them were exactly right.

110
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:08,749
But I was only a kid then.

111
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:12,737
I eventually realized that you have to
have all the facts before hypothesizing.

112
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:15,897
We need to learn everything we
can about the digital world.

113
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:18,377
I know that somewhere down the road we'll

114
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:21,107
be called on again to
help the digital world.

115
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:24,985
Let's just make sure that this
time we're both totally prepared.

116
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,235
All right, listen up.

117
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:29,697
I want you all to meet
back here in two hours.

118
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:30,610
Okay!

119
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:34,433
I told my whole family I would
bring them back souvenirs.

120
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,170
There.

121
00:06:36,253 --> 00:06:37,083
That was fast.

122
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:39,142
Okay, now we can see the sights.

123
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:41,290
Huh?

124
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:44,640
Tell me I'm not seeing
what I think I'm seeing.

125
00:06:55,660 --> 00:07:02,520
I'll demolish them all and once I do my
suffering will finally come to an end

126
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:06,317
yeah whatever stop the talking and keep

127
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,717
destroying I've got a
deadline to meet I haven't

128
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,717
got all day I'm so proud
of that boy sometimes

129
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:15,580
it just makes me want
to cry Terra-Destroyer!

130
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:21,770
Rats!

131
00:07:21,853 --> 00:07:23,040
We got here too late!

132
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:27,530
What's that?

133
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:28,840
It's warping!

134
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,377
The area is starting to become unbalanced.

135
00:07:31,460 --> 00:07:33,837
I saw a warp when he
destroyed the other one, too.

136
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,332
But it was smaller then.

137
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:38,677
It seems like every time Black War
Greymon destroys one of those stones,

138
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:40,637
the warp just gets bigger and bigger.

139
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,955
Hey, look what's happening to him now!

140
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,070
What?

141
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,880
I was right!

142
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,600
It's Black War Greymon!

143
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:06,577
Why is everybody standing
around like nothing's happening?

144
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:08,460
What's wrong with you people?

145
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:23,240
Wait!

146
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:31,177
Stop! You...

147
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:32,780
Digimon? Uh-huh!

148
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:40,300
No! No!

149
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:42,460
No!

150
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:46,680
I am Apemon,

151
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:51,449
I swing into action and use my mega-bone
stick attack to demolish my enemies!

152
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:58,637
I've got to let the others
know what's going on!

153
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,550
Emergency!

154
00:08:59,633 --> 00:09:01,600
Digimon are now in Kyoto! Hurry!

155
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:03,645
Having a wonderful time, Yoli!

156
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:07,697
When will you children ever learn?

157
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:09,368
You can't possibly beat me!

158
00:09:09,780 --> 00:09:10,610
Ha!

159
00:09:10,693 --> 00:09:11,557
We'll see about that!

160
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,581
Let's go, V-mon!

161
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:17,600
Fee-mon Digiball 2!

162
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:23,257
Fee-mon Digiball 2!

163
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:26,240
AXFFEMON Armadillo-mon Digiball 2!

164
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:35,920
AXFFEMON Parrotmon Armored Digiball 2!

165
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:40,640
Armored Digiball Pegasus-mon Flying Hope

166
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:50,920
That's just a legend.

167
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,520
I'm not so sure.

168
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:56,870
Huh?

169
00:09:56,953 --> 00:09:57,783
Wait a minute.

170
00:09:57,866 --> 00:09:59,177
What was that? What do you mean?

171
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:00,357
It was a rehearsal.

172
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,793
That's not what I mean.

173
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:04,020
I just saw something.

174
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:10,400
Get my agent! Good. There he is.

175
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:13,600
Of course, now what am I supposed to do?

176
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:16,480
Ah, good dog?

177
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,280
There it is.

178
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:25,897
All right, Stingmon, do your thing.

179
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:26,810
Right.

180
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:39,640
Stingmon! Yoli!

181
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:41,730
Ken?

182
00:10:41,813 --> 00:10:42,643
I don't get it.

183
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:45,596
I'll explain everything to you later.

184
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:46,630
Stingmon!

185
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:50,697
Remember, he's not a Control Spire
Digimon, so you can't destroy him.

186
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:51,780
Don't worry, Ken.

187
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:01,020
Ken, I got him.

188
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:04,309
All right, Yoli, the
rest is up to you now.

189
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:06,037
What are you talking about?

190
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:06,950
Come back!

191
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:13,090
Okay, Yoli.

192
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:14,197
I'm ready for action.

193
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:15,692
What should we do first?

194
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:18,277
Hey, I thought I left you with Izzy.

195
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,377
What are you doing here?

196
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:21,440
It's a long story. I found her.

197
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:23,168
She's over here, Professor.

198
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:24,437
Excuse me, miss.

199
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:28,020
Are you the girl who called
out Digimon before? Uh, maybe.

200
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:30,420
I have one more question to ask.

201
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,500
What is it?

202
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:34,211
That's a Digimon you're holding, isn't it?

203
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:35,780
Oh, boy.

204
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:55,080
Who are you guys?

205
00:11:55,660 --> 00:11:56,880
Oh, I'm sorry.

206
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:58,297
I'm Professor Takenuchi.

207
00:11:58,380 --> 00:12:00,937
I teach folklore at the
university in Tokyo,

208
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:04,817
but I've been spending the last year doing
research right here in the city of Kyoto.

209
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:05,730
And this is...

210
00:12:05,813 --> 00:12:07,297
My name's Jim, Joe's brother.

211
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:08,557
I'm one of the professor's students.

212
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:12,457
I was pre-med and had to study
everything from brain surgery to bedpans.

213
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:14,837
And then I took one class
from the professor here.

214
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,217
I changed my major to ghosts and goblins.

215
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:19,757
My kid brother still wants
to be a doctor, though.

216
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,670
How nice.

217
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:23,697
I'm Yuli Inui, and I'm in eighth grade.

218
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:25,015
I live in Tokyo, too.

219
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:28,440
But I'm not sure what I'm
doing here. I knew it.

220
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,953
My little brother told me all about you.

221
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:32,630
Huh?

222
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:37,417
Yep, and I've heard a lot of good things
about you from my daughter as well.

223
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:44,160
And, uh, I guess that means that you're
referring to Joe Kido and Sora Takenuchi?

224
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,040
Bullseye! Huh?

225
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,280
The laser!

226
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,140
And now it's my turn!

227
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:57,100
It's V-Man!

228
00:12:57,460 --> 00:12:58,620
Davis, you alright?

229
00:12:59,040 --> 00:12:59,937
Where were you?

230
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:01,079
I've been waiting!

231
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:02,050
Are you ready?

232
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,320
Let's do it! Digimon!

233
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:06,950
Digimon!

234
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,320
X-Beamon!

235
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,130
Stingmon!

236
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:17,060
DNA Digimon II!

237
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:21,610
Hyldramon!

238
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:27,837
I've studied legends all over the world.

239
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:30,920
Loch Ness Monster, Bigfoot,
the Bermuda Triangle.

240
00:13:31,180 --> 00:13:33,237
You should see my frequent flyer miles.

241
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:35,673
Anyway, I don't spend much time at home.

242
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:38,457
I guess that's what caused
Sora to be so angry.

243
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:41,417
And then three years ago, she suddenly
turned into a whole new person.

244
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,097
She and her mother became best friends.

245
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,977
I thought maybe she had a boyfriend or was

246
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:46,837
going through one of those teenage things.

247
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:50,337
But she simply said that she owed
it all to her friends, the Digimon.

248
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:51,900
Her friends, the Digimon?

249
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:53,330
That's right.

250
00:13:53,413 --> 00:13:56,937
Her adventures with them forced her to grow
up and change her outlook on everything.

251
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,177
Especially the stormy
relationship with her mother.

252
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:01,997
You should see them now,
shopping every Saturday.

253
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:04,320
My credit card's at the limit. Oh!

254
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:06,460
So, thanks to the Digimon,

255
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:10,661
our family is a lot closer now,
even though I'm still never around.

256
00:14:11,340 --> 00:14:12,222
You're welcome.

257
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:14,151
That's a beautiful story.

258
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:15,437
Thanks for sharing.

259
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:17,997
I'm glad I'm getting to see a
Digimon on a friendly basis.

260
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,637
I've had a run-in with
them before, you know.

261
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:22,837
When everything happened three years ago,
I was right in the middle of the battle.

262
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,837
Actually, my brother Joe
was a little more involved.

263
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,657
I was sort of helping
out from the sidelines.

264
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:27,877
It's not that I couldn't
have helped them fight,

265
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:30,977
it's just that I wanted to give the
kid a chance to learn on his own.

266
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:32,295
I still don't get it.

267
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:33,897
Of all the cities they could have picked,

268
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:36,877
why did the Digimon start
showing up here in Kyoto?

269
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,997
Ever since Kyoto became the capital,

270
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,897
residents here feel the city has developed

271
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:43,477
a very strong connection
with animal spirits.

272
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,390
What?

273
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:46,050
That's right.

274
00:14:46,133 --> 00:14:47,997
Different animals like raccoons and foxes.

275
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:51,897
One reason I'm here in Kyoto is to determine
if these stories are based on facts.

276
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:55,717
Another reason is there's an outlet mall
where I can get my socks for half price.

277
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,037
I see.

278
00:14:57,120 --> 00:15:00,557
Kyoto was chosen to be
the capital partly because

279
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:03,640
the four gods were in
harmony surrounding the city.

280
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,397
Have you heard that story?

281
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:06,520
I'm not sure.

282
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:08,393
It's quite interesting.

283
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,497
You see, the mountains to the
north are for Genbu the turtle.

284
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,600
The river to the east is
for Sieryu the dragon.

285
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:17,704
The lake to the south is
for Suzaku the phoenix.

286
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:20,780
And the road to the west
is for Byako the tiger.

287
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:22,817
So the city was protected
by the mountains,

288
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:25,097
had the convenience of a
river and roads nearby,

289
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:26,197
and was open to the west.

290
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,377
A perfect scenario.

291
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:28,290
Cool.

292
00:15:28,373 --> 00:15:29,437
There's also the Spirit Gate.

293
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:33,696
And the fact that there were many
temples built in all four directions.

294
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:36,217
They believed that without those temples,

295
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:39,177
it would be too easy for the
magical creatures to get in.

296
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:40,090
Spirits?

297
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:41,690
Creatures?

298
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:43,310
Professor!

299
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:44,820
Oh, I'm sorry.

300
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,557
I didn't mean to scare you.

301
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:49,217
Sometimes I get a little
wrapped up in my own stories.

302
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:51,877
The city has changed a
lot since those days.

303
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:52,790
Anyways,

304
00:15:52,873 --> 00:15:57,660
what I'm trying to say is that Kyoto is
close to the spirit world, in other words,

305
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,597
any world other than our own.

306
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:01,440
Like the digital world?

307
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:05,757
I have a theory that those Digimon you
saw running around found it easier to

308
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:10,237
travel to the warp to the digital world to
Kyoto rather than trying to go to Tokyo.

309
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,150
Wait a minute.

310
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:15,673
Are you trying to tell me that Digimon
are some sort of magical creatures?

311
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:17,557
Well, aren't they? Huh?

312
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:20,257
It's not like they're
just a collection of data.

313
00:16:20,340 --> 00:16:23,957
I believe Digimon are actually legends
that people have spoken of for hundreds

314
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:29,960
of years and over time have gained a level
of consciousness and become a reality.

315
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:35,660
I think that Digimon may have started
as Stata in some old computer,

316
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:37,277
but have since come alive.

317
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:39,140
Just like those old legends.

318
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:41,300
Do you agree with my theory?

319
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:44,300
Uh, huh?

320
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:48,960
Hey, stop the car!

321
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:50,160
There they are!

322
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:58,590
What's that?

323
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:08,697
That's Oceumon, a warrior Digimon
who can take different shapes.

324
00:17:08,780 --> 00:17:12,117
I've seen him use a Shogun sword attack
to make mincemeat out of his enemies.

325
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,977
Should I? Go for it!

326
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:16,140
Four of mine, Digivolve, too!

327
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:18,490
Hawkmon!

328
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:21,740
You can do it, Hawkmon!

329
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:24,357
Do you think Hawkmon will
let me interview him?

330
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,460
Feather strike!

331
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:32,980
Hawkmon, armor Digivolve! Glad to!

332
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:38,660
Digi-Ever-Energize!

333
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:48,400
Pokémon Armor Digivolve, whoo!

334
00:17:48,580 --> 00:17:52,280
Digimon, Digi-o-masters,
Digimon are the champions!

335
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:56,360
Digivolve, you're the champions!

336
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,900
Armor, Digimon!

337
00:18:02,140 --> 00:18:07,380
Digimon, Digi-o-masters, Shurimon,
the samurai of sincerity!

338
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:09,900
Double stars!

339
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:14,497
Professor, do you suggest I start
taking notes about what I'm seeing?

340
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:17,380
Never mind the notes,
drive the car. Right.

341
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:29,520
Professor, do you happen to have
a laptop computer? Um, yeah.

342
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,360
Shogun Sword Double Stars!

343
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:43,340
Cause everything is gone
way too far Digi port, open!

344
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:46,100
Jureimon, the port is open!

345
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:52,600
Jim, close it!

346
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:54,800
He's vanished!

347
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:57,320
No, Jim, he didn't vanish.

348
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:00,621
He returned to the digital
world where he belongs.

349
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:01,630
Ah!

350
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:08,077
You did a good job!

351
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:11,572
But we have to figure out a
way to stop Black War Greymon.

352
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:14,131
Look, Yoli, something's happening to them.

353
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:22,849
They're all returning
to the digital world.

354
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:25,325
Yeah, but I've got a question.

355
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:27,677
Why did they come here to the real world?

356
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:28,760
I don't get it.

357
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:32,197
It may not make sense to us, but
there must have been a reason.

358
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,760
That was really strange.

359
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:38,197
I was able to open the digiport and send
Moosey Yvonne back to the digital world.

360
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,868
But Tai and the others
weren't able to do it.

361
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:41,870
Yoli!

362
00:19:41,953 --> 00:19:42,783
Huh?

363
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:45,337
We better hurry up and get
you back to your class.

364
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:47,877
After all, you don't want to miss
the rest of your school trip, do you?

365
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:49,980
Oh, I almost forgot about that!

366
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:53,830
Huh?

367
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:57,200
They have returned.

368
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:01,300
Mommy Mom, let's go! Right!

369
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:06,880
Going somewhere?

370
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:10,395
I don't have time for a small
talk with small children.

371
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:13,427
I wouldn't get too
comfortable if I were you.

372
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:17,637
There are still five more Destiny Stones
out there, and when I destroy them,

373
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:19,297
there goes the Digital World.

374
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:20,320
Is she serious?

375
00:20:20,660 --> 00:20:23,917
She won't stop until she finds
all of the Destiny Stones.

376
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,977
And if she destroys them all...

377
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:29,457
Then the balance of the Digital
World will be destroyed as well.

378
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:31,060
Now I finally understand.

379
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:33,657
This must be what Izzy was worried about.

380
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:36,660
If the balance of the
digital world is destroyed,

381
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:39,455
something terrible is going to happen.

382
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:42,817
Nice meeting you, Yoli,

383
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:45,917
and be sure to say hi to Sora for
me when you get back to Tokyo.

384
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,180
And to Joe, too. Sure.

385
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:49,740
Nice meeting you.

386
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:52,300
Yoli, where have you been?

387
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:54,857
I had to take care of a
couple of small things.

388
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:56,293
Hey, look, what's that?

389
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:59,369
Uh, just a souvenir,
a very quiet souvenir.

390
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:02,660
Oh, it's so cute.

391
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:04,610
Hey!

392
00:21:04,693 --> 00:21:05,620
Let's go!

393
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:09,140
Sorry about that, Poromon

394
00:21:32,660 --> 00:21:37,100
I'm just going to be thinking about myself

395
00:21:38,660 --> 00:21:40,740
I'm going to connect with my hand

396
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:44,480
I'm going to drive together

397
00:21:45,660 --> 00:21:47,380
Why does it make me so big?

398
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:54,840
Why do you always tell me?

399
00:21:56,220 --> 00:22:01,780
I always tell you how to do it.

400
00:22:02,820 --> 00:22:03,677
I always tell you how to do it.

401
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:08,020
I always tell you how to do it.

402
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:17,940
Thank you.
